@CarlArnold_Scratch1
  +setConversation(Carnold)
  Carnold: "Let's make this quick, I have things to do."
  Assistant: "Right, right..."
  Assistant: "So, um, first thing on the agenda is funding.  We're running a tad low."
  Carnold: "What?  How?"
  Assistant: "Well it's mostly going into repairs at the moment.  General upkeep and all that."
  Carnold: "What's been damaged that costs so much?"
  Assistant: "It's the battles in here, sir.  All these monsters in your instance are causing a lot of havoc and in order to keep certain paths open we need to repair whole sections."
  Assistant: "Not to mention the protestors."
  Carnold: "The protestors are not a concern.  They have no real power here."
  Carnold: "But these monsters? I should've taken care of those a long time ago..."
  Carnold: "Can't we just pay someone to get rid of them?"
  Assistant: "Well, we could, but it would cost a lot more than just repairing the damage."
  Assistant: "I think you'd be better off just taking care of them yourself."
  Carnold: "Hmm.  I don't have time at the moment..."
  Carnold: "Let's put a pin in that for now.  What else is there?"
  Assistant: "Well, there's the complaints of the quality of the food in the cafeteria."
  Carnold: "How is that my problem?"
  Assistant: "The employees say their equipment is breaking down and they can't keep up with the demand."
  Carnold: "And they want me to buy new stuff right?"
  Carnold: "So it's money again."
  Assistant: "Yes, sir."
  Carnold: "Is that going to be the theme of all of the agenda today?"
  Assistant: "I'm afraid so, sir."
  Carnold: "Fine.  I'll take care of it then."
  Carnold: "But I need somebody to look over the <color=PURPLE>Alternate</> I have in the next room over."
  Assistant: "You are speaking of <color=YELLOW>Conscience</>, correct?"
  Carnold: "Yes.  I need someone to make sure she doesn't get out."
  Assistant: "I can do that myself, sir."
  Carnold: "You?  Fine.  She might be more crafty than you think though."
  Carnold: "Just don't open the door for here and you should be fine."
  Assistant: "Yes, sir."
  Carnold: "Now, besides money, is there anything else, or can I go?"
  Assistant: "Well, there is one more thing."
  Assistant: "Bartolo has been giving updates on the whereabouts of that girl <color=YELLOW>Ada</>."
  Carnold: "...yes, and?"
  Assistant: "He says that... um... she's outmaneuvering him a bit."
  Assistant: "Apparantly she found some friends that are helping her out."
  Carnold: "Did he say they were a problem?"
  Assistant: "No, sir.  He says he can handle it.  I just thought that... you should know he sounded slightly nervous."
  Carnold: "Bah.  I can't deal with this.  He has to do his job."
  Carnold: "Maybe I'll take all the Tickets I'm sending him and give them to you to spend."
  Assistant: "I'm not sure that's a good idea, sir."
  Carnold: "Then he'll just have to deal with it."
  +endConversation()

@CarlArnold_ConscienceGone
  +setConversation(Carnold)
  Carnold: "What do you mean she's <shake>gone</>?"
  Assistant: "I'm sorry, sir.  I have let you down."
  Carnold: "But what happened?  Did somebody take her?"
  Assistant: "It is not certain, sir.  Somebody most have opened the door because it could not be opened from the inside."
  Carnold: "And we don't know who?"
  Assistant: "No, sir.  I'm afraid not."
  Assistant: "But we are sure she is still in the instance.  We have been monitoring the exits."
  Carnold: "The exits we know of.  This is all pointing to some kind of breach."
  Carnold: "I will have to look into this myself."
  Assistant: "Would you like me to accompany you, sir?"
  Carnold: "No.  Keep monitoring the exits.  Send a note to Lotte that we might need her."
  Assistant: "She won't be happy about that, sir."
  Carnold: "I don't care.  She told me she'd be here if I needed her."
  Carnold: "Now, I have to go.  I'll be back."
  +endConversation()